<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tokelau</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tokelau is a group of three coral atolls in the South Pacific, north of Samoa, that is a dependent territory of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>. It was annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1916 as part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humphrey-gilbert">Gilbert</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ellice-islands">Ellice Islands</a> Colony and placed under New Zealand administration in 1926, becoming part of New Zealand in 1949. Referendums in 2006 and 2007 narrowly failed to reach the majority needed for self-government in free association.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tokelau.jpg" alt="Tokelau" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown Vector: Andrwsc · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Tokelau.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
